# ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST.
#
# This repository distributes the built plugin's documentation and diagnostic
# tools. It must never contain plugin source, build files, internal working
# documents, or collected diagnostic output describing a real estate.
#
# A denylist of known-bad filenames fails the moment a new one is invented, and
# the failure is silent — the file just gets committed. So everything is ignored
# by default and only the shipping set is un-ignored below.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: a genuinely new public file will not stage until it
# is added here. That is the intended trade. `git status --ignored` shows what
# is being held back.

*

# --- The shipping set -------------------------------------------------------
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!CHANGELOG.md
!FEEDBACK.md
!.gitignore

# Issue forms. Each level must be un-ignored in turn: git will not re-include a
# file whose parent directory is still excluded, so dropping any one of these
# three lines silently loses the templates.
!.github/
!.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
!.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.yml

!docs/
!docs/*.md
!docs/images/
!docs/images/.gitkeep
!docs/images/*.png
!docs/images/*.jpg
!docs/images/*.svg

!tools/
!tools/*.sh
!tools/*.sql

# --- Never, under any circumstances ------------------------------------------
# Restated explicitly so they stay excluded even if the rules above are ever
# loosened. Release artifacts are attached to GitHub Releases, not committed;
# collected diagnostics describe real infrastructure.
release/
*.jar
*.jar.sha256
perch-diag-appliance-*.txt
perch-diag-host-*.txt
perch-diag-db.txt
